# layerpropertycopy

- Label: Layer Property Copy
- Category: Copernicus (`Cop`), Houdini 22.0.368
- Inputs: 0 to 2
- Parameters: 4 (exact, read from Houdini by hython)
- Used by the height graph: no

## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/layerpropertycopy.html
- Summary (EN): The Layer Property Copy node transfers properties from a source layer, VDB or attribute to a destination. The Transfer Properties list selects which properties copy, and toggles select border, type info and precision.
- Résumé (FR) : Copie les propriétés (bord, type d'information, précision) d'une couche, d'un VDB ou d'un attribut source vers une destination.

- Inputs meaning: ["destination: layer, VDB or attribute that receives the copied properties", "source: layer, VDB or attribute that supplies the properties"]

- Key parameters: ["Transfer Properties: list of properties to copy; blank or * copies all, a leading caret excludes listed properties, a caret on the first name copies only unlisted ones", "Transfer Border: copies the border setting", "Transfer Type Info: copies the type info", "Transfer Precision: copies the per-channel storage precision"]

- Caveats: ["Border and precision cannot be transferred between a VDB and a layer in either direction", "Attributes can only transfer their type info to other attributes", "Related nodes Layer Property Create and Layer Property Delete add or remove user-defined properties", "Available since Houdini 22.0"]

